            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Motion Picture Camera</strong><br>\nEdison also played a key role in developing the motion picture camera, contributing significantly to the entertainment industry through his motion picture patents and the development of a film studio.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Electric Power Distribution</strong><br>\nEdison’s work in electricity went beyond invention; he developed an entire electric power distribution system for cities, which included generators, wires, and meters for consumer use.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Patents and Innovation</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Edison received 1,093 U.S. patents for his inventions. His Menlo Park laboratory is often considered the first research and development facility.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
