            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Business Ventures</strong><br>\nEdison founded several companies to manufacture and market his inventions, the most notable being General Electric, which has grown into one of the largest and most diversified companies in the world.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life</strong><br>\nEdison married twice and had six children. His work ethic was legendary, often spending long hours in his lab. His interests and inventions varied widely, showcasing a prolific mind.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact and Legacy</strong><br>\nEdison's inventions have had an enduring impact on the modern world. His legacy lives on in the continuing use of his inventions, which serve as the foundation for many technologies used today.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
